<%# THE DEVOPS SUMMARY CARD — the fourth /deployments summary card: how long a release
    takes, told honestly, and how much work is in flight.

    WHAT IT REPLACED, AND WHY. The old card was six tiles: WIP plus the MEAN of four
    stages and a total over the last ten releases. Measured on production 2026-09-18,
    those numbers were true and still misled: the stages overlap (G3 runs inside
    Assembled, Deployed inside G4), so they never add up; and the mean total, 2h 39m,
    was two outliers — releases that sat open for 6-8 hours collecting work — while
    the median release took about an hour. Release::Flow re-reads the same releases as
    four phases that TILE each release's time, and this card leads with the median.

    FOUR THINGS, top to bottom:
      the typical release     the MEDIAN total — the hero number while nothing is in
                              flight — with the mean beside it, small, so the gap
                              between them is visible (in flight: THE COUNTDOWN below)
      the last ten releases   a sparkline, oldest left, each column stacked by phase;
                              a column past the scale is clipped and marked, so eight
                              ordinary releases are not flattened to a pixel by two
      the typical phases      one bar, each phase's MEDIAN, labelled directly
      the outliers, named     "2 slow releases — most of it in Batch": what the mean hid

    The full story — every release as a row, the phase table, WIP by stage, and the
    original six stage averages — opens in the sidebar (tasks/_devops_detail).

    A BROADCAST SLOT (#devops-summary-card): DeploymentsBroadcaster.devops_card
    re-renders it over the "deployments" stream whenever the in-flight release changes
    phase — prepare (a release opens), QA green (assembled), ship start, shipped,
    abandoned — so the clocks below are re-estimated live. Its WIP count is read at
    that render too, so a task move alone does not refresh it.

    THE COUNTDOWN. While a release is in flight (estimate, a Release::Flow::Estimate)
    the hero is no longer history but a clock: the time left until that release
    should land in production — what it has spent, plus the rest of the median of
    the phase it is in, plus the medians of the phases after it — ticked each second
    by devops_countdown.js off data-deadline, with the clock time under it ("lands
    ~2:45 PM MT"). Past its estimate it counts the overrun up, "+12m over", in the
    warning ink. On the right, over the sparkline, a smaller QA clock counts to QA
    green (the end of the QA phase) and disappears once QA is green. The line under
    the hero is then the RUNNING AVERAGE (the mean). With
    nothing in flight the card is exactly as it was: the median, "typical release".
    The estimate is server-side, so a phase change re-renders the card (above) rather
    than leaving a page-load clock to read "+Xm over"; the ticker is delegated, so
    the swapped card keeps ticking with nothing to re-arm.

    Locals: flow (Release::Flow or nil), estimate (Release::Flow::Estimate or nil),
            wip_count, wip_by_stage %>
<% flow = local_assigns[:flow] %>
<% estimate = local_assigns[:estimate] %>
<% wip_count = local_assigns[:wip_count] %>
<%= tag.div(**deploy_summary_card_options("devops", test: "devops-summary-card", id: "devops-summary-card")) do %>
  <%= render "tasks/summary_card_header", panel: "devops", title: "DevOps",
             meta: wip_count.nil? ? nil : "#{wip_count} in flight" %>

  <% if flow&.any? %>
    <% median = flow.median_total %>
    <% mean = flow.mean_total %>
    <% outliers = flow.outliers %>
    <% scale = flow.scale_seconds %>
    <div class="mt-3 flex items-end justify-between gap-3">
      <% if estimate %>
        <%# The ticking clock is hidden from screen readers, which hear the estimate once
            in the sr-only line, never each tick. Text only: it updates under reduced
            motion too. %>
        <div class="min-w-0" data-test="devops-countdown" data-phase="<%= estimate.phase %>"
             data-gem-history="<%= estimate.gem_history %>">
          <div class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold leading-none tabular-nums text-heading data-[eta-kind=over]:text-warning-ink"
               data-test="devops-eta" aria-hidden="true"
               data-devops-countdown data-countdown-over
               data-deadline="<%= estimate.eta.utc.iso8601 %>"
               data-eta-kind="<%= estimate.over? ? "over" : "left" %>"
               data-remaining="<%= estimate.remaining %>"><%= release_countdown_text(estimate) %></div>
          <span class="sr-only">
            <%= estimate.over? ? "The release is #{release_flow_duration(estimate.overrun)} past its estimate" : "The release should land in about #{release_flow_duration(estimate.remaining)}" %>,
            around <%= release_landing_clock(estimate.eta) %>.
          </span>
          <div class="mt-1 text-2xs leading-tight text-muted">
            running avg <span class="tabular-nums text-secondary" data-test="devops-mean"><%= release_flow_duration(mean) %></span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-2xs leading-tight text-muted">
            <span class="whitespace-nowrap" data-test="devops-landing"><%= estimate.over? ? "due" : "lands" %> ~<time datetime="<%= estimate.eta.utc.iso8601 %>"><%= release_landing_clock(estimate.eta) %></time></span>
            <span class="whitespace-nowrap" data-test="devops-current-phase">· in <%= estimate.phase_label %></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <div class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold leading-none tabular-nums text-heading" data-test="devops-typical"
               data-seconds="<%= median %>"><%= release_flow_duration(median) %></div>
          <div class="mt-1 text-2xs leading-tight text-muted">
            typical release <span class="whitespace-nowrap">· avg <span class="tabular-nums" data-test="devops-mean"><%= release_flow_duration(mean) %></span></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# THE RIGHT COLUMN: the QA-green clock over the sparkline while the in-flight
          release has not reached QA green; then the sparkline alone, as always. %>
      <div class="flex shrink-0 flex-col items-end gap-1.5">
        <% if estimate&.qa_pending? %>
          <%# THE QA CLOCK — the same estimator stopped at the end of QA (assembled_at):
              when the release should be QA-green. Smaller than the hero; gone once QA
              is green. Ticked by devops_countdown.js like the hero, "+Xm over" past it. %>
          <div class="text-right leading-none" data-test="devops-qa-countdown">
            <span class="text-3xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">QA in</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm font-bold tabular-nums text-heading data-[eta-kind=over]:text-warning-ink"
                  data-test="devops-qa-eta" aria-hidden="true"
                  data-devops-countdown data-countdown-over
                  data-deadline="<%= estimate.qa_eta.utc.iso8601 %>"
                  data-eta-kind="<%= estimate.qa_over? ? "over" : "left" %>"
                  data-remaining="<%= estimate.qa_remaining %>"><%= release_qa_countdown_text(estimate) %></span>
            <span class="sr-only">QA should be green around <%= release_landing_clock(estimate.qa_eta) %>.</span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <%# THE SPARKLINE. Oldest left, newest right. Each column is one release, its height
            its total against the tallest ORDINARY release (Flow#scale_seconds); a column
            past that scale is drawn full height with a 2px surface break near its top —
            the axis-break mark — so its length is admitted, not implied. %>
        <div class="flex h-10 shrink-0 items-end gap-[2px]" role="img"
             aria-label="Last <%= flow.size %> releases, oldest first: <%= flow.chronological.map { |e| release_flow_duration(e.total) }.join(", ") %>"
             data-test="devops-sparkline">
          <% flow.chronological.each do |entry| %>
            <% clipped = outliers.include?(entry) %>
            <% height = clipped ? 100 : [(entry.total.to_f / scale * 100).round, 6].max %>
            <div class="relative flex w-2 flex-col-reverse gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-t-sm"
                 style="height: <%= height %>%"
                 data-test="devops-spark-column"
                 data-release="<%= entry.slug %>"
                 data-clipped="<%= clipped %>"
                 title="<%= entry.slug %> · <%= release_flow_duration(entry.total) %><%= " — off the scale" if clipped %>">
              <% Release::Flow::PHASE_KEYS.each do |key| %>
                <% seconds = entry.phase(key) %>
                <% next if seconds.zero? || entry.total.zero? %>
                <div class="<%= release_flow_phase_class(key) %> w-full" style="flex: <%= seconds %> 1 0px; min-height: 1px"></div>
              <% end %>
              <% if clipped %>
                <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-1.5 h-0.5 bg-surface" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# THE TYPICAL PHASES — each phase's median, as one bar with 2px surface gaps and a
        label under every segment, so identity never rides on colour alone. %>
    <% medians = Release::Flow::PHASES.map { |phase| [phase, flow.phase_median(phase[:key]).to_i] } %>
    <% medians_total = medians.sum(&:last) %>
    <div class="mt-3" data-test="devops-phase-bar">
      <div class="flex h-2 w-full gap-0.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full">
        <% medians.each do |phase, seconds| %>
          <% next if seconds.zero? || medians_total.zero? %>
          <div class="<%= release_flow_phase_class(phase[:key]) %> h-full first:rounded-l-full last:rounded-r-full"
               style="flex: <%= seconds %> 1 0px"
               title="<%= phase[:label] %> · typically <%= release_flow_duration(seconds) %> — <%= phase[:hint] %>"></div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-2.5 gap-y-0.5 text-3xs leading-tight text-secondary" data-test="devops-phase-legend">
        <% medians.each do |phase, seconds| %>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" data-test="devops-phase" data-phase="<%= phase[:key] %>" data-seconds="<%= seconds %>"
                title="<%= phase[:hint] %>">
            <span class="<%= release_flow_phase_class(phase[:key]) %> h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-sm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <%= phase[:label] %> <span class="tabular-nums text-heading"><%= release_flow_duration(seconds) %></span>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# WHAT THE MEAN WAS HIDING, named. Only when there is something to name. %>
    <% if outliers.any? %>
      <% dominant = outliers.map(&:dominant_phase).tally.max_by { |_phase, count| count }&.first %>
      <% dominant_label = Release::Flow::PHASES.find { |phase| phase[:key] == dominant }&.dig(:label) %>
      <p class="mt-auto pt-2 text-2xs leading-tight text-muted" data-test="devops-outlier-note">
        <span class="font-medium text-heading"><%= pluralize(outliers.size, "slow release") %></span>
        (<%= outliers.map { |entry| release_flow_duration(entry.total) }.join(", ") %>)<% if dominant_label %> — most of it in <%= dominant_label %><% end %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted" data-test="devops-empty">No shipped releases yet.</p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
